  <div class="slide caption-page" data-document-role="page" data-label="C1 - Caption (copy/paste)">
    <div class="caption-flag">Caption - not for posting</div>
    <div class="caption-body">When your child covers their ears in a loud room, their brain may be reacting to that sound the way most brains react to a real threat.<br><br>In sensory over-responsivity, brain areas tied to threat and emotion can over-activate in response to ordinary input, and the brain is slower to get used to, or habituate to, repeated stimulation. So the hum, the echo, the overlapping voices can register as something to defend against rather than tune out.<br><br>That is not an overreaction they are choosing. It is a brain responding at full volume to input other people filter automatically. Understanding that changes the whole moment. Not too sensitive. Wired to react.</div>
    <div class="caption-tags">#sensoryoverresponsivity #auditorysensitivity #amygdala</div>
    <div class="caption-accounts">Tag: none needed</div>
  </div>


