  <div class="slide caption-page" data-document-role="page" data-label="C2 - Caption (copy/paste)">
    <div class="caption-flag">Caption - not for posting</div>
    <div class="caption-body">Your brain runs a constant filtering process most people never notice. Researchers call it sensory gating.<br><br>Sensory gating is how the brain screens out unimportant background input, the hum of the fridge, the tag on your shirt, so you can focus on what matters. In some children, that filter lets more through than usual. When it does, the world simply arrives louder, brighter, and busier than it does for other people.<br><br>So a sensitive child who seems overwhelmed by a busy room is not choosing to notice everything. Their brain is not screening it out the way most brains do. They are taking in what other nervous systems quietly filter away. The filter is set differently, not broken.</div>
    <div class="caption-tags">#sensorygating #filtering #sensoryoverresponsivity</div>
