  <div class="slide caption-page" data-document-role="page" data-label="C3 - Caption (copy/paste)">
    <div class="caption-flag">Caption - not for posting</div>
    <div class="caption-body">When a sensitive child seems to feel everything more intensely, brain research suggests they genuinely are processing more deeply.<br><br>Studies of high sensitivity find greater activation in brain regions tied to awareness, empathy, and depth of processing. So the same moment that rolls off another child can register more deeply and vividly in a sensitive one. That depth is where their perceptiveness and empathy come from.<br><br>It is also why a loud, busy room drains them faster than it drains other kids, because their brain is doing more with everything it takes in. The very trait that overwhelms them is the one that makes them so tuned in. Depth of processing is a real strength that comes with a real cost.</div>
